// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1091716912" "You've taken control of the Blood Coral for yourself!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4268303160" "Brilliant work, {HeroName}! The Blood Coral is safe and sound in our own warehouse and the Legacy Chain is battered and beaten! I couldn't ask for anything better. The fools will soon see that the day they exiled me was the day they destroyed themselves! What did you think of the Blood Coral that was formed already? Was it beautiful? Magnificent?<br><br>I wish I could see it, truly I do, but... I must ignore the calls that it sends to me, the whispers in my mind. I know what they are a symptom of. If I were to get near the fully formed Blood Coral, I fear I would lose myself entirely. But you, {HeroName}, you have not been poisoned as I have. You are immune to the call, which is why you will attain great power all too soon. We just need to simply go after the Coralax lair and recover the last pieces! Then we will have all the Blood Coral needed to control the Leviathan!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Lorenz 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P1579966514" "What's up, {HeroName}? Been a while since you and me talked, was beginning to wonder if you were backin' off of what we agreed on. So you found Joey was dead huh? Can't say I'm too upset about that, rat was tryin' to turn on us, he deserves to get himself dead.<br><br>Anyway, this whole thing gives me an idea, and I'm a man who thrives on gettin' ideas. We had a number of cargo shipment that went missin' recently. Only problem is, we're usually the ones that makes things go missin'. Lucky for us, we had ourselves a little trackin' beacon on the cargo, 'cept we don't know <i>what</i> the cargo is. If we can find the cargo and see what it is, we're gonna catch the other mook who's been workin' with the Legacy Chain red handed."
// Answer Text :
"P1895621850" "How is the cargo going to prove anything?"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P1997436193" "Easy, {HeroName}, here's the thing. We got some generic kinda beacons on the cargo, yeah? Cheaper to make that way. Lotta the cargo we lost recently was 'cause of the Legacy Chain. But this one piece of cargo, it looks like it washed up into some sorta underwater cavern, like someone <i>took</i> it there or somethin'.<br><br>Weird, huh? Anyway, we know who is usually set to guard our shipments and what they're guardin' specifically. I figure, we find out what was in that cargo, we can pin the guy who was guardin' it as our man. I got the rough location of where the cargo is. Gimme a ring when you got yourself in a cavern nearby and I'll letcha know if you're near the cargo."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Vince 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P2055184099" "Hey, {HeroName}, been wondering where you went off to. Mr. Cage's guards got that Scrapyarder to sing all kinds of songs about what the Legacy Chain are up to. You hear about this <color yellow>Blood Coral</color> business? Seems like some pretty crazy stuff. Even Mr. Cage says he doesn't want anything to do with it, and Mr. Cage isn't the kind of guy to back away from something. I figure he knows <i>something</i> about it, but he isn't telling me.<br><br>Anyway, we still got ourselves a problem now with the Legacy Chain <i>and</i> the Coralax. That Thom guy was talking about how they were helping the Legacy Chain sneak into the Rogue Isles by keeping quiet about all the magic guys hidden in the crates they carry. Turns out they've been hijacking ships that the Family have. <br><br>Now, that whole thing is something that the Family and that guy Lorenz Ansaldo is gonna handle. Me and you, we're gonna handle the issue with the Scrapyarders and the Coralax."
// Answer Text :
"P3097555142" "What about the Coralax?"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P1287648652" "Check this out. Turns out the Legacy Chain claim that the Coralax got this artifact that'll make whoever holds it super strong, or something. Thom kept wavering on it, saying it was psychic, super strong, one time he even mentioned it could make ya teleport. Whatever it is, the Legacy Chain got the Scrapyarders convinced that this is their ticket outta the pits, which is why I'm guessing they're helping out the Legacy Chain.<br><br>Thom said that someone tracked it down to some sorta underwater cavern or somethin' crazy like that. I need ya to go check it out and see if you can nab this artifact before those goons in the Scrapyarders can. Give a ring when you're in that cavern and I'll let you know what the artifact is supposed to look like."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Maros 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P3395550628" "You have found the journal of Barracuda and have seen that her heart still has some warmth in it. The others around her are unaware of this and she has tried to deny this as much as possible. It is a sad fate and one that she will not uncover the answer for, at least not during this time. But there is a note in there that could cause some issue to you. Does the Blood Coral cause you to turn into a Coralax?<br><br>Surely, if it did, you would be one already, considering your exposure. There must be more to it and more to the Blood Coral. I say this because I have <i>seen</i> that there is more to it, but I could not simply tell you what it is. However, I am not so cruel as to say this without having a method for you to move forward to your new place in time."
// Answer Text :
"P2487982353" "Well...?"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P3537079196" "You are going into an underwater cavern, full of Coralax. Somehow, a spirit of the Banished Pantheon roams the caverns. The Coralax leave it be, but it has observed much of their actions and their behaviors, more than most mortals. This spirit is able to see the connections that these Coralax have to the Red Coral. If you were to shatter this spirit's connection to this world, you would gain the knowledge it has and see what it sees. Do this, and you shall also see what I see.<br><br>I should warn you, however. I have seen the futures of Barracuda, and one of them involves her also discovering the location of this cavern. <color orange>If you wish to avoid your future coming to an abrupt end, I would prepare for a fight against her if you enter those caverns.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Leonard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P1992453137" "{HeroName}, the journey continues, does it not? Where do you believe this path to power will lead you? To fortune? To glory?<br><br>This is a question that I asked Thomas Mane many times. He believed that we would one day discover that 'one thing' that would lead us to greatness. Even after many of our investigations into legends of old led to dead ends, he always kept that belief that there was something else to be had. It was amiable, if foolish.<br><br>Perhaps our problem was that we lacked power to go that extra distance; it seems you, in a short amount of time, have stumbled upon bit after bit of ground-breaking power. I remember at a certain point, we attempted to track down the <color yellow>Order of the Four Winds</color>. I believed that I could recover one of the mantles, such as the one Scirocco bears, and lead Mane Corp into untold power. As you can see, that did not... pan out. But I go on, once again. What is it that is happening this time, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P3227863349" "(Explain to Leonard the situation with the Coralax.)"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P742468686" "A lost underwater cavern? This should be very interesting. I should have no problem reaching you once give me the proper signal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OptionalContacts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Vince Text :
"P3098068008" "That artifact has got to be somewhere in there, {HeroName}. Check out if you can find it, cause if those Scrapyarders were doing all this just to get <i>that</i>, it must be something big."
// Answer Text :
"P1029810121" "Roger."
// Page Lorenz Text :
"P338696552" "You're in the right area, {HeroName}. The cargo should be somewhere nearby. All you gotta do is check out what's in it and we'll have the answers we're looking for."
// Page Maros Text :
"P76164514" "The mask of the Banished Pantheon wanders those halls, {HeroName}. But beware, the potential paths in Barracuda's future have all narrowed to one; her arriving to try to kill you when you gain the knowledge within that mask."
// Answer Text :
"P3054950304" "I'll keep that in mind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2830324928" "We have little else to speak about, {HeroName}. All that's left is to go into the caves that the Coralax inhabit and recover the three remaining pieces of Blood Coral. When that is done, we can merge them with what we have already and begin our conquest of Sharkhead Isle and the Legacy Chain!<br><br><color orange>While the prospect of unlimited power may be at your fingertips, there seem to be many odd happenings during your short time with Vincent; the whisper from the Blood Coral, Vincent's possible 'disease', and his fear of getting taken over by the Blood Coral. Many people have been destroyed in the past by not understanding the power they're taking. You'll have to look for more research on this Blood Coral in the Coralax cavern to prevent yourself from meeting the same fate.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P1335834460" "I'll get it handled, make sure the runes remain strong."
// SendOffString :
"P247671682" "I shall, {HeroName}. I won't have much to fear from the Legacy Chain for the moment, given the sound beating you just gave them. Hah! What a terrific feeling it is, I only <i>wish</i> I could've seen how much you beat them down! Now, just as a fair warning, these Coralax caves are rumored to hold <color yellow>Shapers</color>. They're considered the figures of authority in the Coralax society, ever since their goddess, <color yellow>Merulina</color>, vanished. They're a little more powerful than your average fish, and I'm betting they'll be holding onto the Blood Coral.<br><br><color DeepSkyBlue>Those who have been working together with other factions should contact the factions representative at this time.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2020098515" "Raid the Coralax Cave"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3278326311" "Hrm? Oh, I'm just thinking over the look on the faces of those Legacy Chain fools when we're done with them!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1484314710" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: There's Always a Catch</color>"

