// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1678917025" "{HeroName}! Give us back the Blood Coral!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - CoralaxBoss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1131356933" "We will only regain our glory through the Blood Coral. We must find the secret of its power and spread it to our champions!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1950398641" "You do not deserve to have the Blood Coral, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - CoralaxBoss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2901204182" "You've retrieved all the pieces of the Blood Coral and learned that the plan that Vincent Ross had might not go so smoothly after all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2662928115" "It's done! The final pieces obtained! {HeroName}, we are at the pinnacle of destroying those fools!<br><br>What?<br><br>It's... not going to control the Leviathan? Is this some cruel joke? That's impossible! It's supposed to control the beast, it's supposed to do what we need it to do! How could I have missed this in my research... I thought I found everything, <i>everything</i>! It must've been those traitors in the Legacy Chain... <i>they</i> knew I was onto something, <i>they</i> hid the research from me! Of course... it all makes sense now. I was blind not to see it before.<br><br>Maybe there would be a way for you to gain power through the Leviathan, but what good would it do us if you were taken over? We'd need a way to stop that, but not even the Coralax have found it yet! But... wait... the Midnight Squad. Yes... yes that could be it!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Lorenz 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P1013529818" "What's up, {HeroName}? You find that shipment?<br><br>Yeah? Buncha guns and ammo and Superadyne? Along with <i>two</i> tracking devices, one from Longbow!<br><br><color orange>Lorenz lets out a string of curses in Italian for a good minute before calming down.</color><br><br>That idiot! Man, {HeroName}, this here is <i>bad</i>. The guy guarding the crates? The one who looks like he's in cahoots with the Legacy Chain <i>and</i> Longbow? It's my <i>own brother</i>, Alexander Ansaldo! All the luck, huh? I always knew that kid was gonna lead to somethin' bad, I just didn't think he was <i>that</i> stupid to try to backstab me.<br><br>He thinks he's doin' what's right, huh? Well, that's where he's wrong. Kids got it all wrong, tryin' to betray family like that. Now, I gotta handle this before the big wigs back in Paragon hear about this, namely <color yellow>Sebastian Frost</color>, guy who is the head of the Family."
// Answer Text :
"P499573094" "By mean you handle this, I assume you mean me."
// Page Page2 Text :
"P604948630" "Heh heh... well, yeah. Now, I ain't gonna go bemoan the fact that you gotta kill my kid brother. Fact of the matter is that I told him, warned him not to even think about betrayin' us, but now he went and <i>ignored</i> what I said <i>and</i> is tryin' to get me killed. I figure for that, he ain't my brother anymore. He's just another pig that's gotta be gutted, and I'm givin' you the knife to do it.<br><br>Too bad he ain't knowin' that I placed a little trackin' device on him too; always figured I'd use it to spring him outta prison instead of tryin' to see where he is to kill him. Now, let's see... huh. Weird. Looks like he's in some sorta unmarked office buildin' nearby. Here's the address.<br><br><color orange>The address that Lorenz gives you is the same one as the Midnighter Office.</color><br><br>Now, I don't care <i>why</i> he's there. All I care about is that he gets killed, yeah? You do that, you get your payday and my eternal gratitude, or somethin'. Gimme a call when you get in there and I'll tell you where this pig is located."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Vince 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P1733169755" "You find that artifact, {HeroName}? Wha? It isn't powered?<br><br>Hah! I gotta laugh about that, those Scrapyarders got led on a wild goose chase by the Legacy Chain, huh? That doesn't mean you and me can't see how this can benefit the Cage Consortium still. All we got to figure out is how to power that thing up, right? Should be simple enough.<br><br>Now, you handled things with stopping them Scrapyarders from working with the Legacy Chain, so Mr. Cage is letting me transfer funds to you as we speak. You figure out a way to get that artifact working and Mr. Cage will offer you a hefty sum of money if it's something that's gonna be useful."
// Answer Text :
"P2230519183" "I might just have an idea, Vince."
// Page Page2 Text :
"P1296086261" "<color orange>You explain to Vince Dubrowski that you're going to be inside of a Midnighter's Club building and that you might be able to find something in there.</color><br><br>See, this here is why you're going to be the Cage's go to super for things, {HeroName}. When you get into that office, you contact me and I'll tell you just how much Mr. Cage is willing to offer you if this artifact turns out to be useful."
// Answer Text :
"P3045747775" "Will do, Vince."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Maros 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P2543356689" "The paths come closing in now. You've seen what the spirit has seen, what I have seen, and crushed Barracuda's hope beneath your heel. The Coralax believe this Blood Coral is their true link to Merulina, though you also know by now that the Blood Coral is a direct link to the Leviathan. It seems they believe this Leviathan to be a reincarnation of Merulina, that she awaits to take control of the beast. This is utter nonsense. <br><br>The Leviathan is a beast of destruction and chaos, while Merulina was known to be a goddess of peace and harmony. It is unfortunate that time has made her creations, the Coralax, into the monstrous beasts that they are today. However, let us go over the facts. Perhaps not so much for yourself, but so that I may grasp which time we are in.<br><br>We have understood that the Blood Coral channels more of the Leviathan's power. This is done through a ritual to earn the respect of the Leviathan to allow more of its power to go inside of the coral. The coral itself is seen by the Coralax as a direct connection to Merulina. And yet... it is possible that the Coralax have used this Blood Coral to infect the woman we now call Barracuda. There is only one dangling issue, it seems. How is it possible to earn the respect of a being that has been sleeping all of this time?"
// Answer Text :
"P3346584772" "... Do you have an answer to that question?"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P761904789" "I see the possible answer, but it is one you must discover. The demon you will meet, the one within the Midnighter's office. I am... quite familiar with it.  You see, {HeroName}, I was the one who summoned Botis into this world, and it was through that ritual that my spirit was split across the time streams. This demon is even older than I and has knowledge of a millenia.<br><br>You seek its knowledge as to how to protect yourself from being absorbed. I suggest you inquire as to <i>what</i> exactly is behind the Leviathan. Do this, and you shall come one step closer to possessing the secrets behind this Blood Coral. There is no need for you to use the radio device to contact me, simply speak with the demon and look for a chance to find more information."
// Answer Text :
"P1187696371" "We'll see what happens."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Leonard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P2403025888" "It seems like things are progressing with your plans, {HeroName}. It is interesting to see how much success you are having regarding all of this, I must say.<br><br>Thomas Mane and I came close to uncovering one of the great secrets of our time: the true location of the Island of Mu. Some say that the Rogue Isles are the islands, but there was no conclusive facts to back that up. Our research took us nearly all over the world, until we came upon an ancient library where we believed the location of Mu was held, along with the secrets behind the Leviathan. Unfortunately for us, we were set upon by creatures of pure darkness, the likes of which I have never seen.<br><br>We were forced to retreat, and the passage to the library lost forever. A depressing end, one that I hope you do not find in your own journeys. Speaking of, what is the next goal?"
// Answer Text :
"P3861707440" "(Explain to Leonard the Midnighter's office)"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P3991020163" "Hrm, I see. A daring idea to go against the Midnighters. I've no issue with it, however. Simply inform me of when to arrive, as usual, and I will do so."
// Answer Text :
"P2559484788" "Finish"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OptionalContacts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Vince Text :
"P267020882" "Hey, {HeroName}. Make sure you find whatever you can to power up that artifact thing. Mr. Cage has got a good amount of money set aside for you if this thing turns out to be something we can use."
// Page Lorenz Text :
"P4233374829" "Alexander's in that place for sure, {HeroName}. Gut him like the pig he is and end this thing once and for all."
// Page Leonard Text :
"P3447255354" "This world is full of super villains. They want to do evil things like take over the world."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DemonDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2951610993" "{HeroName}. Do not be surprised. I know that you know who I am. I know of your deeds here within the Rogue Isles. And I know what you come here to seek. Do you see, {HeroName}, that I am bound here? The Midnighters have gone to great lengths to see that I am here to serve them, to show them the secrets of the past and the possibilities of the future. Much like yourself.<br><br>I shall give you my aid, {HeroName}, in exchange for your help in setting me free."
// Answer Text :
"P648571982" "... I'm supposed to believe a demon's word?"
// Page Believe Text :
"P3364649866" "My word is all that I have, {HeroName}. That, and the vengeance I wish to enact on those who have bound me into this place."
// Answer Text :
"P24133100" "Tell me the information, and then I'll free you. That's the deal."
// Page Deal Text :
"P1181389376" "<color orange>Botis glares at you.</color><br><br>Very well, {HeroName}. But before we begin, I shall give you a glimpse of what would happen, should you try to go back on your word.<br><br><color orange>You see a number of images flash before your eyes, as if a part of you were travelling through time. You see yourself betraying Botis, and Botis moving to attack you. In the battle, you notice Botis is unable to damage the artifacts that keep him bound. You watch Botis kill you and siphon your power for his own use. The images fade and you're able to see clearly.</color><br><br>Now, I believe we have an understanding."
// Answer Text :
"P2993301494" "... Tell me what I need to know."
// Page Leviathan Text :
"P4045616047" "The Leviathan's power is immense, yes, but there is a ritual that can be enacted to prevent it from taking over one's mind. <br><br><color orange>A scroll appears in your hand, detailing the ritual.</color><br><br>There is a far greater power behind the Leviathan. You could say that the Leviathan is linked to it; this being is the origin of the Leviathan's power. What exactly that being is, and where the power comes from, is a mystery even to me. All that is known is that this being rewards knowledge and power to those who have earned it. Those who do not... are destroyed.<br><br>Those who overcome the obstacles within the Leviathan will be granted the knowledge that not even I have; the truth behind the Leviathan's power and the method to acquire it for yourself."
// Answer Text :
"P328933367" "Is that it?"
// Page DecisionPage Text :
"P3284173025" "That is it. Now, we have a deal, {HeroName}. I have given you what you want, now you are to give me what I want."
// Answer Text :
"P2915937961" "Sorry, Botis, but I'll take my chances. I won't be freeing any demon today."
// Answer Text :
"P1445877566" "A deal is a deal. I'll get you out of here."
// Answer Text :
"P3652935866" "Before that, I want to know more about what is behind the Leviathan's power."
// Page Maros Text :
"P1394165532" "<color orange>Botis sneers at you.</color><br><br>You reek of Maros. Does the fool still remain split amongst time?<br><br>I shall share more of what I know of this power. The entity behind the Leviathan is ever present, always looking to give power to those who earn it. It may have even given the Leviathan its own power when Calystix summoned it.<br><br> It is not an evil entity, nor is it good. It is simply a being that respects power and grants it to those who have earned its notice.<br><br>If there is more to this entity, I do not know it, as it is a being that is older than even myself."
// Answer Text :
"P3757359219" "Hrm... Interesting..."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2564906649" "Then you shall die for your treachery!"
// Answer Text :
"P2222563272" "Here we go...!"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1404343977" "Excellent. I eagerly await my freedom, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P429474978" "I'll make sure you get it, trust me."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Wade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KnowWade Text :
"P4082983913" "Well, {HeroName}, looks like you and I are bound to keep running into each other, eh? Curious about my research into Rularuu, or are you here to make a deal?<br><br>I still haven't forgotten your help in 'replacing' those artifacts with the Midnight Squad."
// Answer Text :
"P2875114161" "(Explain to Darrin the information you need)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P523190684" "Hrm... information on the Leviathan, eh? Sure, why not? That beast has been asleep for centuries. All the attempts I've heard to awaken it have ended in failure, though I would rather the Midnight Squad <i>not</i> have any knowledge on it. It is true that they have a method to find more about the Leviathan, though they have not used it yet. It isn't so much a book, as it is a <i>creature</i> that they have. You see, the Midnighters use the Isles to conduct activities that the authorities in Paragon would...frown upon. One such activity is the containment of a demon named <color yellow>Botis</color>.<br><br>Don't ask how I've come about this information, as there's several little sources I have in the Midnighters. This Botis is a demon that has a condition similar to <color yellow>Diviner Maros</color>. It can see both the present and the past. Rumor is that it's a timeless demon, but that's another story. The demon is being bound in one of the Midnighter's offices here in Sharkhead Isle, and few in the Midnighter's even know of its existence. They're keeping it there as a resource for forbidden knowledge. I think our Leviathan friend would count as that, eh? Here's the location of the office, but there's one thing you should be aware of. The Midnighters are guarding this secret very heavily. <color orange>The office has various portals that connect each of the levels. If you choose the wrong portal, you'll end up in a cavern full of the Midnighter's guardian spirits.</color> There should be members of the Midnighter's in there that have notes on which portals are the right one. Anyway, that's all, and remember, you didn't get this information from me. But when the time comes, remember, <i>you got this information from me</i>. Do we have an understanding?<br><br><color DeepSkyBlue>Those who have been working together with other factions should contact the factions representative at this time.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2080060529" "I believe we do."
// Page DontKnow Text :
"P40765738" "Hrm, who would you  be? If you're talking to me, then you know who I am, at least by name. I've seen many things in my lifetime, events that would cause most men to question the very fabric of reality. Lucky for me, I'm not like most men; what I've seen has just made me want <i>more</i>, you see.<br><br>I'm a man with a lot to get done, so let's make this quick about what you want."
// Answer Text :
"P1016301788" "(Explain the situation to Wade)"
// Page KnowWadeNotComplete Text :
"P1510810682" "Looks like we meet again, {HeroName}. Doing work for others, are we? That's fine, but just remember, you and I still have work to do against the Midnighters. If you're not here to deal with <i>my</i> situation, what are you here for?"
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P764595232" "The Leviathan? Interesting project, but why should I help you? This is the Isles, a place of give and take, and I'm not a man who is quite willing to be charitable right now, if you get my drift. Besides, I have no interest myself in the beast, so whatever you find down there won't be of any use to me. I'm sure you wouldn't be willing to help someone without them helping you first, right? What can you offer me to give you this information?"
// Answer Text :
"P1337014645" "(Offer the Coralax book 'Ancient Knowledge')"
// Answer Text :
"P928495539" "I'm not giving you anything for this, Wade."
// Page NotGiving Text :
"P1781071539" "Oh yeah? So I'm just supposed to give you this information for free, am I?"
// Answer Text :
"P3042191844" "You want the Midnighters to be weakened, don't you? This will do it."
// Page MidnightersWeakened Text :
"P2132856370" "<color orange>Darrin Wade grins.</color><br><br>You got a way with words, {HeroName}. I respect that. I'll tell you what you need to know, as long as you go rough on the Midnighters you find in that office."
// Answer Text :
"P2562100399" "I'm listening."
// Page AncientKnowledge Text :
"P1976860194" "<color orange>You hand the Coralax book labeled 'Ancient Knowledge' to Darrin Wade. He flips through it for a few moments, nodding to himself.</color><br><br>The Coralax have always fascinated me. This knowledge of theirs could go a long way towards some plans of mine... alright, {HeroName}. You've got yourself a deal. I'll tell you what you need to know."
// Page DarrinExplain Text :
"P2125965551" "It is true that the Midnight Squad have a method to find more about the Leviathan, though they have not used it yet. It isn't so much a book, as it is a <i>creature</i> that they've recently acquired. You see, the Midnighters use the Isles to conduct activities that the authorities in Paragon would...frown upon. One such activity is the containment of a demon named <color yellow>Botis</color>.<br><br>Don't ask how I've come about this information, as there's several little sources I have in the Midnighters. This Botis is a demon that has a condition similar to <color yellow>Diviner Maros</color>. It can see both the present and the past. Rumor is that it's a timeless demon, but that's another story. The demon is being bound in one of the Midnighter's offices here in Sharkhead Isle. They're keeping it there as a resource for forbidden knowledge. I think our Leviathan friend would count as that, eh? Here's the location of the office, but there's one thing you should be aware of. The Midnighters are guarding this secret very heavily. <color orange>The office has various portals that connect each of the levels. If you choose the wrong portal, you'll end up in a cavern full of the Midnighter's guardian spirits.</color> There should be members of the Midnighter's in there that have notes on which portals are the right one. Anyway, that's all, and remember, you didn't get this information from me. But when the time comes, remember, <i>you got this information from me</i>. Do we have an understanding?<br><br><color DeepSkyBlue>Those who have been working together with other factions should contact the factions representative at this time.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2787052209" "I've delt with the Midnight Squad in the past, though not a terrible amount. They tend to believe the Legacy Chain are beneath them. They're right, of course, the Legacy Chain just do parlor tricks, spinning their wheels to the tune of their pathetic ideas. The Midnight Squad is not any better, but they're much more powerful and much more learned.<br><br>Unfortunately for us, they're also much more secretive. If the Midnight Squad somehow holds the secret to protecting <i>you</i> from the control of the Leviathan, we'll need to find out where that secret is and how to get it. In all my power, I'm unable to help you with this, but I know someone who can."
// AcceptString :
"P2901895560" "Who is it?"
// SendOffString :
"P1567044028" "A man named <color yellow>Darrin Wade</color>. Perhaps you've heard of him. He's a clever man, a former member of the Midnight Squad. He holds many of their secrets still and has done battle with them on occasion. He resides here in Sharkhead now, an outcast, much like myself. There are many things that Wade desires, and one of them would be the destruction of the Midnight Squad. Speak with him about what you're looking for, and perhaps he'll be able to help you. Just be warned that he thinks very... <i>highly</i> of himself. He may be difficult to deal with. Just make sure you keep it general, we don't want him to know that you might be able to gain the power of the Leviathan. All Wade needs to know is that we want to steal information on the Leviathan."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3711235687" "<color deepskyblue>Part Four: The Path to Knowledge</color>"

